.TH "SLIPWAY-GET" "1" "" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-get \- Display one or many resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway get"
.I "(TYPE [NAME...] | TYPE/NAME...)"\&
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display one or many resources.
.PP
Prints a table of the most important information about the specified resources. You can filter the list using a label selector and the \-\-selector flag. Projects are listed in the current group unless you pass \-\-all\-groups.
.PP
Use \-o wide to add the path, the head commit, the age of the last commit and the drift of each project: the ways its repository differs from its manifest and what keeps sync from converging it. Use \-o json or \-o yaml for the full object with its status.
.PP
Resource types: projects (project, proj) and groups (group). Type words are case\-insensitive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. One of: table, wide, json, yaml, name. (default "table")
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (label query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', '!=', 'in', 'notin' (e.g. \-l key1=value1,key2=value2,key3 in (value3)). Matching objects must satisfy all of the specified label constraints.
.TP
\fB\-\-field\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (field query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', and '!=' (e.g. \-\-field\-selector key1=value1,key2=value2). Projects support metadata.name, metadata.group, spec.path, status.state, status.branch, status.lastFetch; groups support metadata.name. Values compare exactly, case included, with the object \-o json prints: spec.path as registered, status.lastFetch as an RFC 3339 time. A field the object leaves out compares as the empty value, except status.lastFetch, which compares as never. A backslash escapes a backslash, a comma or an equals sign in a value.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-all\-groups\fR
If present, list the requested object(s) across all groups. The group in the current configuration is ignored even if specified with \-\-group.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
When using the default output format, don't print headers.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-labels\fR
When printing, show all labels as the last column.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# List all projects in the current group
slipway get projects
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List all projects in every group, with the path and last commit
slipway get projects \-A \-o wide
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List a single project in YAML output format
slipway get project hldr \-o yaml
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List the projects labeled lang=rust
slipway get projects \-l lang=rust
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List the projects in every group that are not clean
slipway get projects \-A \-\-field\-selector status.state!=Clean
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List the projects no fetch has reached
slipway get projects \-\-field\-selector status.lastFetch=never
.EE
.PP
.EX
# List every group
slipway get groups
.EE
